{
  "info": {
    "name": "BRL Task 4 — Real-Time Support Desk API",
    "description": "Complete API documentation for the Real-Time Support Desk.\n\n**Setup**\n1. Set `baseUrl` (default http://localhost:5000).\n2. Run **Auth → Login (saves token)** — it stores `{{authToken}}` automatically.\n3. Run **Tickets → Create ticket (saves ticketId)** — it stores `{{ticketId}}`.\n4. For agent/admin requests log in with the matching demo account:\n   - user@support.test / Demo@123\n   - agent@support.test / Demo@123\n   - admin@support.test / Demo@123\n\nEvery protected request sends `Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:5000" },
    { "key": "authToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "adminToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "agentToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "ticketId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "agentId", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Authentication",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register — success (201)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('Returns token and user', () => {",
                  "  const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(b.token).to.be.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(b.user.role).to.equal('user');",
                  "  pm.expect(b.user).to.not.have.property('password');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "auth", "register"] },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"New Person\",\n  \"email\": \"new.person@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"secret123\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Creates a normal user account. Password is hashed with bcrypt before storing. Role always defaults to `user` from the API.\n\n**201** → token + user\n**400** → missing fields / short password\n**409** → email already registered"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Register — validation error (400)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": ["pm.test('Status 400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));"],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "auth", "register"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"email\": \"someone@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"123\"\n}" },
            "description": "Missing name and a password shorter than 6 characters → **400**."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Register — duplicate email (409)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": ["pm.test('Status 409 Conflict', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));"],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "auth", "register"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Duplicate\",\n  \"email\": \"user@support.test\",\n  \"password\": \"secret123\"\n}" },
            "description": "Registering with an existing email → **409 Conflict** (unique index in MongoDB)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login — success (saves token)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('authToken', b.token);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', b.user.id);",
                  "pm.test('authToken saved for following requests', () => pm.expect(b.token).to.be.a('string'));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "auth", "login"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"user@support.test\",\n  \"password\": \"Demo@123\"\n}" },
            "description": "Verifies the password with bcrypt and returns a JWT valid for 1 day. The test script stores it as `{{authToken}}`.\n\nChange the email to `agent@support.test` or `admin@support.test` to switch roles.\n\n**401** → wrong email or password (same message for both)"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login — invalid credentials (401)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": ["pm.test('Status 401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "auth", "login"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"user@support.test\",\n  \"password\": \"wrong-password\"\n}" },
            "description": "Wrong password → **401** with a generic message so we never reveal which field was wrong."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get current user /me (200)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('No password in response', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().user).to.not.have.property('password'));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{authToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "auth", "me"] },
            "description": "Protected route example — requires `Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get /me — no token (401)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": ["pm.test('Status 401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "auth", "me"] },
            "description": "Protected resources must reject unauthenticated requests → **401**."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get /me — expired/invalid token (401)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": ["pm.test('Status 401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.not-a-real-token", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "auth", "me"] },
            "description": "A garbage/expired JWT → **401 Invalid or expired token**."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Tickets",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create ticket (saves ticketId)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const t = pm.response.json().ticket;",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('ticketId', t._id);",
                  "pm.test('Ticket starts as OPEN / MEDIUM', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(t.status).to.equal('OPEN');",
                  "  pm.expect(t.priority).to.equal('MEDIUM');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{authToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/tickets", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "tickets"] },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Cannot reset my password\",\n  \"description\": \"The reset email never arrives.\",\n  \"category\": \"Account\",\n  \"priority\": \"HIGH\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Any logged-in user creates their own ticket. Saves `_id` as `{{ticketId}}`.\n\n**201** → created ticket\n**400** → missing title/description or invalid priority\n**401** → not logged in"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create ticket — missing fields (400)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": ["pm.test('Status 400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));"],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{authToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/tickets", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "tickets"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"No description here\"\n}" },
            "description": "Missing description → **400**."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create ticket — invalid priority (400)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": ["pm.test('Status 400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));"],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{authToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/tickets", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "tickets"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Test\",\n  \"description\": \"Test\",\n  \"priority\": \"URGENT\"\n}" },
            "description": "Priority outside LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH → **400** (validated in the route and by the Mongoose enum)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List tickets — pagination + filters",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Returns pagination metadata', () => {",
                  "  const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(b).to.have.all.keys('page', 'limit', 'totalPages', 'totalItems', 'results');",
                  "  pm.expect(b.results).to.be.an('array');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{authToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/tickets?status=OPEN&priority=HIGH&search=email&page=1&limit=10",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "tickets"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "status", "value": "OPEN", "description": "OPEN | IN_PROGRESS | RESOLVED | CLOSED" },
                { "key": "priority", "value": "HIGH", "description": "LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH" },
                { "key": "search", "value": "email", "description": "matches title or description (case-insensitive)" },
                { "key": "page", "value": "1" },
                { "key": "limit", "value": "10", "description": "max 50" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Role-scoped listing** — the server decides what each role sees:\n- `user` → only tickets they created\n- `agent` → only tickets assigned to them\n- `admin` → all tickets\n\nAll query params are optional."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List tickets — invalid status filter (400)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": ["pm.test('Status 400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));"],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{authToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/tickets?status=WHATEVER",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "tickets"],
              "query": [{ "key": "status", "value": "WHATEVER" }]
            },
            "description": "Unknown status filter → **400**."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List tickets — no token (401)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": ["pm.test('Status 401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/tickets", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "tickets"] },
            "description": "Unauthenticated listing → **401**."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get ticket by id (200)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": ["pm.test('Status 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{authToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{ticketId}}", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "tickets", "{{ticketId}}"] },
            "description": "Allowed for the creator, the assigned agent, and any admin. Others get **403**."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get ticket — not found (404)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": ["pm.test('Status 404 Not Found', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));"],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{authToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/64b000000000000000000000", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "tickets", "64b000000000000000000000"] },
            "description": "Well-formed but non-existent id → **404**."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get ticket — forbidden (403)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": ["pm.test('Status 403 Forbidden', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));"],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{agentToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{ticketId}}", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "tickets", "{{ticketId}}"] },
            "description": "Log in as `agent@support.test` (Agent → Agent Token script) first. An agent who is not assigned to this ticket gets **403**.\n\nKnowing an id is not enough — the backend checks ownership on every request."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update ticket details (200)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": ["pm.test('Status 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{authToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{ticketId}}", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "tickets", "{{ticketId}}"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Cannot reset my password (updated)\",\n  \"priority\": \"HIGH\"\n}" },
            "description": "Only the ticket creator (or an admin) can edit, and not after closing → otherwise **403** / **400**."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update status — agent/admin (200)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Status changed', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().ticket.status).to.equal('IN_PROGRESS'));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{agentToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{ticketId}}/status", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "tickets", "{{ticketId}}", "status"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"IN_PROGRESS\"\n}" },
            "description": "Roles: `agent` (assigned tickets only) and `admin` (any ticket).\n\nThe change is saved over REST **and broadcast** to the ticket room as `ticket_updated`, so every open client updates instantly."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update status — invalid value (400)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": ["pm.test('Status 400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));"],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{agentToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{ticketId}}/status", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "tickets", "{{ticketId}}", "status"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"DONE\"\n}" },
            "description": "Invalid ticket status → **400**."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update status — as normal user (403)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": ["pm.test('Status 403 Forbidden', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));"],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{authToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{ticketId}}/status", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "tickets", "{{ticketId}}", "status"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"RESOLVED\"\n}" },
            "description": "RBAC: a plain `user` is not allowed to change status → **403** (checked in the backend, not the frontend)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Assign to agent — admin (200)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Assigned and moved to IN_PROGRESS', () => {",
                  "  const t = pm.response.json().ticket;",
                  "  pm.expect(t.assignedTo).to.not.equal(null);",
                  "  pm.expect(t.status).to.equal('IN_PROGRESS');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{adminToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{ticketId}}/assign", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "tickets", "{{ticketId}}", "assign"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"agentId\": \"{{agentId}}\"\n}" },
            "description": "Admin only. Get `{{agentId}}` from **Admin → List agents**. An OPEN ticket becomes IN_PROGRESS when assigned.\n\nUse `{{adminToken}}` (run **Agent Token → Admin Token** script first)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Assign — as non-admin (403)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": ["pm.test('Status 403 Forbidden', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));"],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{authToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{ticketId}}/assign", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "tickets", "{{ticketId}}", "assign"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"agentId\": \"{{agentId}}\"\n}" },
            "description": "Only admins may assign → **403** for user/agent tokens."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Assign — non-agent id (404)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": ["pm.test('Status 404 Not Found', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));"],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{adminToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{ticketId}}/assign", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "tickets", "{{ticketId}}", "assign"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"agentId\": \"{{userId}}\"\n}" },
            "description": "Assigning someone who is not an agent (uses your own `{{userId}}`) → **404 Support agent not found**."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Close ticket (200)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Ticket is CLOSED', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().ticket.status).to.equal('CLOSED'));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
